# Allowlist: ~/.claude is full of runtime state and secrets that Claude Code
# creates and renames across versions. Ignore everything by default so new
# state files can never be committed by accident; tracking something new is a
# deliberate opt-in below.
/*
!/.claude
!/.devcontainer
!/.github
!/.gitignore
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/justfile
!/lefthook.yml
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/references
!/skills

!/bin
!/lib

# `!/skills`, `!/bin` and `!/lib` un-ignore everything beneath them, build
# output included. These tighten the allowlist back up; they are not an
# exception to it.
/skills/**/obj/
/skills/**/bin/
/bin/**/obj/
/bin/**/bin/
/lib/**/obj/
/lib/**/bin/

# Same tightening for `!/.claude`. That directory is this repo's *project*
# scope — the repo root doubles as `~/.claude`, so user-scope settings.json
# sits at the root and stays untracked, while the permissions a contributor
# needs to run `just check` here live one level down and ship with the repo.
# settings.local.json is personal by definition, so re-ignoring everything and
# naming the one tracked file keeps it out even if it reappears.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
